  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a sequence aaa and its first nnn elements.\n\nThe iii-th element of the sequence, where i&gt;ni &gt; ni&gt;n is generated by the following formula.\n\nThe iii-th element i&gt;ni &gt; ni&gt;n would be the floor of the mean of the last nnn elements of the sequence. Formally,\n\nai=⌊∑k=0n−1ai−n+kn⌋a_i = \\left\\lfloor \\frac{\\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} a_{i-n+k}}{n} \\right\\rfloorai​=⌊n∑k=0n−1​ai−n+k​​⌋\n\nFor example,\n\nan+1=⌊a1+a2+⋯+ann⌋a_{n+1} = \\left\\lfloor \\frac{a_1 + a_2 + \\dots + a_{n}}{n} \\right\\rflooran+1​=⌊na1​+a2​+⋯+an​​⌋\nan+2=⌊a2+a3+⋯+an+1n⌋a_{n+2} = \\left\\lfloor \\frac{a_2 + a_3 + \\dots + a_{n+1}}{n} \\right\\rflooran+2​=⌊na2​+a3​+⋯+an+1​​⌋\nan+3=⌊a3+a4+⋯+an+2n⌋a_{n+3} = \\left\\lfloor \\frac{a_3 + a_4 + \\dots + a_{n+2}}{n} \\right\\rflooran+3​=⌊na3​+a4​+⋯+an+2​​⌋\n\nYou have to answer many queries in which you would be asked to tell some xxx-th element of the sequence, where xxx would be provided in the query.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nFirst line will contain TTT, the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nFirst line of each test case contains an integer nnn.\nThe second line of each test case contains nnn space-separated integers where the iii-th integer denotes the value of aia_iai​.\nThe third line contains an integer QQQ denoting the number of queries.\nEach of the next QQQ lines contains an integer xxx, denoting that you should tell what's the xxx-th element of the sequence.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each query, output an integer denoting the value of the corresponding element of the sequence.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤101 \\leq T \\leq 101≤T≤10",
      "1≤n≤1031 \\leq n \\leq 10^31≤n≤103",
      "For 1≤i≤n1 \\leq i \\leq n1≤i≤n, 1≤ai≤1031 \\leq a_i \\leq 10^31≤ai​≤103",
      "1≤Q≤1051 \\leq Q \\leq 10^51≤Q≤105",
      "1≤x≤1091 \\leq x \\leq 10^91≤x≤109"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
